class:: SpecSparsity
summary:: Hoyer spectral sparsity
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/SpecCentroid2

description::
For M selected bins returns (sqrt(M) - sum(w)/sqrt(sum(w.squared))) / (sqrt(M)-1). A flat nonzero vector is 0 and a vector with a single occupied bin is 1; silence is 0. One selected nonzero bin returns 1.

For these formulas w is the raw FFT magnitude or its square, and f is the bin-center frequency in Hz. Silence returns 0. The reader preserves the FFT chain. Hoyer (2004), Non-negative Matrix Factorization with Sparseness Constraints, equation 1. Source: link::https://www.jmlr.org/papers/volume5/hoyer04a/hoyer04a.pdf::.

CPU cost is linear in the number of FFT bins; no memory is allocated while processing. It adds no lookahead beyond the upstream FFT. At a 1024-sample window and 48 kHz the initial analysis window is about 21.3 ms. Changing FFT size or window affects unnormalized values.

Like vanilla link::Classes/SpecCentroid::, this reads FFT frames and produces control-rate timbre information; this class measures hoyer spectral sparsity instead of the average frequency.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: chain
FFT chain from an FFT with the same literal fftSize. New-frame values update the output; between frames the previous output is retained.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest included bin center in Hz; default 0 includes DC.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest included bin center in Hz; 0 selects Nyquist. Empty ranges return 0.

argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 uses magnitude; literal 1 uses squared magnitude (power).

argument:: fftSize
Literal power of two from 256 through 8192. Must match the FFT buffer.

returns::
One control-rate descriptor value.

examples::
The descriptor opens a low-pass filter: stronger descriptor values make the sample brighter. The mapping is deliberately bounded so the result stays audible on this recording.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot {
    Routine({
        var buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
        s.sync;
        ~mir2Example = {
            var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, buffer, BufRateScale.kr(buffer), loop: 1);
            // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
            var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
            var feature = SpecSparsity.kr(chain, fftSize: 1024);
            var amount = Lag.kr(feature.clip(0, 1), 0.08);
            var cutoff = amount.linexp(0, 1, 250, 6500);
            var fade = Line.kr(0, 1, 0.15);
            (RLPF.ar(source, cutoff, 0.6) * 0.18 * fade) ! 2
        }.play;
        ~mir2Example.onFree { buffer.free };
    }).play(AppClock);
};
)

// Stop the example and release its sample buffer.
(
~mir2Example.free;
)
::

